@startuml
title A payment endpoint — a name resolves to commitments, never to an address
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ParticipantBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam ActorBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam ActorBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam LifelineBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F5F9FF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

actor Alice as A
participant "Token\ncontract" as TOK
participant "Lookup channel\nfile, ENS record\nor registry" as LOOK
actor Bob as B
participant "Relayer\ncontract" as REL

== Ahead of time, by the recipient ==
A -> TOK : initialize_transfer_commitment(\n  to = alice, completer = relayer)  x N
TOK -> TOK : partial_i = H(alice, randomness_i)\nwrite H(partial_i, relayer)
TOK --> A : c1, c2, c3, ...
A -> LOOK : publish alice.aztec -> [c1, c2, c3]
note over A, LOOK #F5F9FF
  Alice's address is inside each hash, blinded
  by fresh randomness. The list reveals nothing
  about who owns it.
end note

== At payment time, by any sender ==
B -> LOOK : resolve alice.aztec
LOOK --> B : c2
B -> B : sign an authwit for the relayer\nto move exactly this amount
B -> REL : pay_private(token, c2, amount, nonce)
REL -> TOK : transfer_private_to_commitment(\n  from = bob, c2, amount)
TOK -> TOK : msg_sender is the relayer,\nso H(c2, relayer) checks out
TOK -> TOK : debit Bob, complete the note to Alice
note over REL, TOK #F5F9FF
  The relayer is the completer, so any sender can
  pay. Bob is the debited `from`, so the relayer
  never holds or is pre-funded with his tokens.
end note
TOK --> A : Alice's PXE finds the completion log\nfor c2 and removes it from pending
note over A #F5F9FF
  Alice did nothing at payment time, and never
  learned who Bob is. c2 must now be pruned from
  the list: completing it twice loses the money.
end note
@enduml
